---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { LinkButton } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";
import newToEsphomeImg from "../../assets/images/homepage/new-to-esphome.webp";
---

<section class="new-to-esphome card-bgc">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-container">
      <h2>New to ESPHome? Read this!</h2>
      <p>
        Every ESPHome device is built around a small, inexpensive chip called a microcontroller – commonly an ESP32
        (hence the name ESPHome!), but it also works with others like the Raspberry Pi RP2040. The chip is the
        programmable part that controls your sensors, switches, and displays. ESPHome creates the programming that runs
        on the chip, telling it what to do. Once installed, the chip can then “talk” directly to Home Assistant or any
        other smart home system that supports it.
      </p>

      <Image src={newToEsphomeImg} alt="New to ESPHome" layout="constrained" />

      <LinkButton href="/install/">Get started</LinkButton>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  @use "../../styles/mixins" as *;

  .new-to-esphome {
    img {
      max-height: 100%;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      @include fluid(16, 32, $property: margin-top);
      @include fluid(16, 32, $property: margin-bottom);
    }
  }
</style>
